messages:
dana: quick heads-up — opened a tiny docs PR to tweak the SDK snippets for streaming + retries + pagination across py/ts/go. main changes: recommend small-batch defaults, add an explicit KV-cache hint, and clarify backoff math. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4823 :eyes:

jess: linking now. is this just examples or do we need runtime changes too?

michael: just docs. snippets only. i added a short python example for streaming with retry/backoff and KV cache usage. please sanity-check the API names (we used client.stream() and StreamOptions.kv_cache_hint).

michael: ```python
# python streaming example (recommended pattern)
with client.stream("gpt-4o-mini") as s:
    s.send("summarize: ...", options={"batch_size": 8, "kv_cache_hint": "session:invoice"})
    for chunk in s:
        process(chunk)
# on retry, re-use the kv_cache_hint + resume token
```

jess: looks good. one nit: add a short note on aborting / finally closing stream to avoid leaked sockets.

michael: added that note and a tiny TS snippet too.

michael: ```ts
// typescript streaming example
const s = client.stream('gpt-4o-mini', { batchSize: 8, kvCacheHint: 'session:invoice' })
try {
  s.send('summarize: ...')
  for await (const chunk of s) {
    handle(chunk)
  }
} finally {
  await s.close() // ensure resources freed
}
```

kai: quick ask on pagination: if a user combines streaming and paginated retrieval, we should show how resume tokens interplay with KV cache. maybe a tiny diagram or one-line bullet.

jess: agreed, put a one-liner under "Retries & resumption": "When resuming, pass the last resume_token and the same kv_cache_hint to avoid duplicated context."

michael: pushed that language. also added a tiny Go example showing manual backoff/backoff jitter pseudo-code.

michael: ```go
// go streaming sketch
s, err := client.Stream("gpt-4o-mini", StreamOptions{BatchSize:8, KVCacheHint:"session:invoice"})
if err != nil { log.Fatal(err) }
defer s.Close()
for {
  chunk, err := s.Recv()
  if err == io.EOF { break }
  if err != nil {
    backoff := computeJitteredBackoff(retries)
    time.Sleep(backoff)
    continue
  }
  process(chunk)
}
```

dana: awesome, thanks. can someone do a quick pass for wording and link fixes? i'm gonna request review from @jess and @michael and merge once CI preview looks ok. :rocket:

jess: i'll review in ~2h.

